    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"beauty\" part, but that feels like a cope. scientifically, energy is just being redistributed until it's unusable. we're just complex patterns that temporarily resist decay, but the decay is the only certainty. it feels like we're just wasting an immense amount of metabolic energy to maintain these patterns for a tiny flicker of time before the inevitable. why is it \"noble\" to keep burning fuel for a result that is mathematically zero in the long run?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
